## Run
```
python scripts/run_{{pkg}}_{{part}}.py --input <file.h5ad> --outdir <dir> [--from-run <upstream run dir>]
```
Through the pinned environment: `bin/omicstat-r-route.sh python skills/{{module}}/scripts/run_{{pkg}}_{{part}}.py ...`
(omicstat-py image). A direct run writes the figure REQUEST only; the figures are drawn by
`bin/omicstat-r-route.sh Rscript skills/_shared/scripts/render_figure_request.R --run-dir <dir>` (omicstat-r).

Every flag, its type and its default come from one spec in the entry script (`SPEC`,
`_shared/py/ospy/args.py`); `--help` prints it in the suite-wide format. Invalid input stops with a
typed error (`OS_UNKNOWN_FLAG`, `OS_MISSING_PARAMETER`, `OS_INVALID_PARAMETER`,
`OS_CONFLICTING_PARAMETERS`, `OS_HANDOFF_*`, `OS_ECOSYSTEM_MIXED`). Warnings raised by the engine are
kept in `qc/engine_warnings.csv`.

### Via MCP
Call `omicstat_run` with `module="{{module}}"` and the same flags as `args`; the shell runs the
Python entry in omicstat-py and then the R render step in omicstat-r, and returns one manifest.
